The data
The PSID has followed about 5,000 US families since 1968, and keeps interviewing their children once they form households of their own. Three downloads are used:

the cross-year individual file (ind2023er): one row per person, identified by the 1968 family number ER30001 and person number ER30002, with the interview number, sequence number, relation to the reference person and age in each wave;
the Parent Identification File (pid23): each person’s birth mother and father;
a Data Center family extract: labor income of the reference person (RP) and spouse in the 2017 to 2023 waves, which refers to calendar years 2016, 2018, 2020 and 2022.

py/01_prepare.py reads the needed columns from the 560 MB individual file and writes three small CSVs. PSID data cannot be redistributed, so none of these files are in the repository.
